Ques14:
Compare polling and interrupt-based programming in embedded systems. In which situations would interrupts significantly improve the
performance of an IoT device? 
Ans – In polling, the microcontroller continuously checks whether an event has occurred, which wastes CPU time. In interrupts, the 
microcontroller performs other tasks and responds only when an event occurs. Interrupts are better for time-critical applications like fire
alarms, motion detection, or emergency buttons because they provide a faster response.
